Package: rsageMissing
Title: Missing Data Analysis Module for R Sage
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("R Sage contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@rsage.dev")
Description: Summarises and visualises missing values in a data frame,
    tests whether they are missing completely at random, and imputes them.
    Exploration uses 'naniar'; when 'naniar' is not installed the module
    falls back to its own summaries and 'mice'. Imputation uses 'mice'.
    analyse() returns an 'rsage' result that prints in the console and
    renders in Quarto documents.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: rsage (>= 0.1.0), dplyr, tibble, ggplot2, rlang, stats
Suggests: naniar, mice, UpSetR, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
